{"files": [{"id": 20049944, "name": "jz9b02868_si_001.pdf", "size": 1268687, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/20049944", "supplied_md5": "72188018bbea3e8313009652a58638c7", "computed_md5": "72188018bbea3e8313009652a58638c7", "mimetype": "application/pdf"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 8072765, "full_name": "Paulo\nC. T. Souza", "first_name": "Paulo\nC. T.", "last_name": "Souza", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 1339593, "full_name": "Sebastian Thallmair", "first_name": "Sebastian", "last_name": "Thallmair", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 135518, "full_name": "Siewert J. Marrink", "first_name": "Siewert J.", "last_name": "Marrink", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 1717771, "full_name": "Rau\u0301l Mera-Adasme", "first_name": "Rau\u0301l", "last_name": "Mera-Adasme", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://acs.figshare.com/articles/journal_contribution/An_Allosteric_Pathway_in_Copper_Zinc_Superoxide_Dismutase_Unravels_the_Molecular_Mechanism_of_the_G93A_Amyotrophic_Lateral_Sclerosis-Linked_Mutation/11312432", "download_disabled": false, "description": "Several different mutations of the protein copper, zinc\nsuperoxide\ndismutase (SOD1) produce the neurodegenerative disorder amyotrophic\nlateral sclerosis (ALS). The molecular mechanism by which the diverse\nmutations converge to a similar pathology is currently unknown. The\nelectrostatic loop (EL) of SOD1 is known to be affected in all of\nthe studied ALS-linked mutations of SOD1. In this work, we employ\na multiscale simulation approach to show that this perturbation corresponds\nto an increased probability of the EL detaching from its native position,\nexposing the metal site of the protein to water. From extensive atomistic\nand coarse-grained molecular dynamics (MD) simulations, we identify\nan allosteric pathway that explains the action of the distant G93A\nmutation on the EL. Finally, we employ quantum mechanics/molecular\nmechanics MD simulations to show that the opening of the EL decreases\nthe Zn\u00ad(II) affinity of the protein. As the loss of Zn\u00ad(II) is at the\ncenter of several proposed pathogenic mechanisms in SOD1-linked ALS,\nthe structural effect identified here not only is in agreement with\nthe experimental data but also places the opening of the electrostatic\nloop as the possible main pathogenic effect for a significant number\nof ALS-linked SOD1 mutations.", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 1268687, "created_date": "2019-12-03T20:46:48Z", "modified_date": "2023-06-13T03:33:22Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 10, "name": "CC BY-NC 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/"}, "tags": ["Allosteric Pathway", "EL detaching", "protein copper", "SOD 1.", "neurodegenerative disorder amyotrophic", "opening", "zinc superoxide dismutase", "G 93A mutation", "EL decreases", "MD", "G 93A Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis-Linked Mutation", "ALS-linked SOD 1 mutations", "ALS-linked mutations", "SOD 1", "Zn", "allosteric pathway", "loop", "SOD 1-linked ALS", "multiscale simulation approach", "mechanism", "Zinc Superoxide Dismutase Unravels", "Molecular Mechanism", "metal site"], "keywords": ["Allosteric Pathway", "EL detaching", "protein copper", "SOD 1.", "neurodegenerative disorder amyotrophic", "opening", "zinc superoxide dismutase", "G 93A mutation", "EL decreases", "MD", "G 93A Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis-Linked Mutation", "ALS-linked SOD 1 mutations", "ALS-linked mutations", "SOD 1", "Zn", "allosteric pathway", "loop", "SOD 1-linked ALS", "multiscale simulation approach", "mechanism", "Zinc Superoxide Dismutase Unravels", "Molecular Mechanism", "metal site"], "categories": [{"id": 1